      "writtenOn": "2024-05-04T00:14:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Updated the comment to be more descriptive. Please take a look.\n\n\u003e Btw, could I know the use case of having a sorted SdkKind set? Since there is no subset/superset relationship, I am not sure if true sorting is even possible.\n\nI\u0027m trying to implement a check that verifies that the module does not link against a stub of a wider api scope. The order should generally determined based on the recursive iteration of [`apiScope.extends`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/sdk_library.go;drc\u003d00e0991f702751098fe95c0dfce5cd3725659abf;l\u003d75), but [not all `SdkKind` has a corresponding `apiScope`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/sdk_library.go;drc\u003d00e0991f702751098fe95c0dfce5cd3725659abf;l\u003d421), thus I believe that having this \"general trend\" of the `SdkKind`s can assist determining the closest `apiScope` for the `sdkKind` that does not exist in `allApiScopes`.\n\nI\u0027ll send out the change that implements the check once it\u0027s ready, and maybe we can continue the discussion there?",
